#7. A weather monitoring system records temperature and humidity over five days. The temperature values are [22, 25, 28, 30, 32], and the humidity values are [80, 75, 68, 60, 55]. Write a Python program to calculate the covariance matrix of temperature and humidity, and to visualize their relationship with a scatter plot.
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

temp = [22, 25, 28, 30, 32]
humidity = [80, 75, 68, 60, 55]

C = np.cov(temp, humidity)
print("Covariance Matrix:\n", C)

plt.scatter(temp, humidity)
plt.xlabel("Temperature")
plt.ylabel("Humidity")
plt.title("Temperature vs Humidity")
plt.grid()
plt.show()
